      "problem": "Simplify the expression $3\\sqrt{80} -8\\sqrt{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we use the product rule for radicals to simplify $\\sqrt{80},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{80} & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 5}=\\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{80}-8\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 3(4\\sqrt{5})-8\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 12\\sqrt{5}-8\\sqrt{5}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can combine the two $\\sqrt{5}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12\\sqrt{5}-8\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ (12-8)\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 4\\sqrt{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
